Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: opt in to the highest fractional monitor scale

Keep native Wayland buffer scales and XSettings UI scales integral. Use the
highest monitor scale for the shared X11 geometry, rendering, damage and input
coordinates when xwayland-native-resolution is enabled with automatic scaling.

diff --git a/data/org.gnome.mutter.wayland.gschema.xml.in b/data/org.gnome.mutter.wayland.gschema.xml.in
--- a/data/org.gnome.mutter.wayland.gschema.xml.in
+++ b/data/org.gnome.mutter.wayland.gschema.xml.in
@@ -149,6 +149,17 @@
       </description>
     </key>
 
+    <key name="xwayland-native-resolution" type="b">
+      <default>false</default>
+      <summary>Use the highest monitor scale for Xwayland without rounding up</summary>
+      <description>
+        Experimental local option: use the highest monitor's fractional scale
+        for the shared Xwayland coordinate space instead of rounding it up.
+        Applies in logical layout mode with automatic Xwayland scaling. Outputs
+        at lower scales are resampled. This affects all X11 windows. Log out
+        after changing this option.
+      </description>
+    </key>
     <key name="xwayland-scaling-factor" type="d">
       <default>0</default>
       <summary>Configure the Xwayland scaling factor</summary>
